  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Rohde and Schwarz Usa obligated $424M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Rohde and Schwarz Usa received 72 awards so far, with an average award size of $5.9M. Rohde and Schwarz Usa obligations are up 235.7% year over year. Rohde and Schwarz Usa saw large, concentrated buying from the Department of Transportation, which obligated $403M, dominating the company\u0019s FY2026 to date totals. Rohde and Schwarz Usa earned the bulk of its FY2026 to date obligations in the Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing market, which accounted for $403M. Historical obligations for Rohde and Schwarz Usa show a ramp from $20.2M in FY21 and $25M in FY22 to $56.2M in FY23, with a dip to $35.3M in FY24 followed by $126M in FY25 before the current-year jump to $424M. Rohde and Schwarz Usa also recorded smaller FY2026 to date obligations in Instrument Manufacturing for Measuring and Testing Electricity and Electrical Signals ($8.8M) and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing ($8.4M).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top agency buyers of Rohde and Schwarz Usa?",
        "body": "Department of Transportation is the top buyer, obligating $403M in FY2026 to date. Department of Defense is the second buyer, obligating $18.6M. Department of Commerce, Department of Homeland Security, NASA, and HHS follow with $1.4M, $434K, $251K, and $126K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which product and market categories drive Rohde and Schwarz Usa revenue?",
        "body": "Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing is the largest market, accounting for $403M in FY2026 to date. Instrument Manufacturing for Measuring and Testing Electricity and Electrical Signals and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing are material secondary markets, accounting for $8.8M and $8.4M respectively. Several smaller markets each contribute under $1.2M, including Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $1.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
